==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*maþô}}, from Indo-European ''*math-, *moth-'' used for insects and vermin. Cognate with Old Saxon [[maðo]] (Dutch [[made]] ‘maggot, worm’), Old High German [[mado]] (German [[Made]] ‘maggot’), Gothic [[𐌼𐌰𐌸𐌰]]; Old Norse had the diminutive form [[maðkr]] (dialectal English [[mawk]]; compare also [[maddock]]). The Indo-European root is also the source of Old Armenian {{m|xcl|մաթիլ||small louse}}.

